The chemical structure in the image can be represented using LaTeX with the `mhchem` package for chemical formulas. Here is the LaTeX code to represent the structure:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{mhchem}

\begin{document}

\[
\ce{H2N-C(=O)-c1cc(O)c(C)c(C)-c(=O)N2}
\]

\end{document}
```

This code will produce a chemical structure similar to the one in the image. Note that the `mhchem` package is used to handle the chemical notation, and the structure is written in a way that LaTeX can interpret and render correctly.

The chemical formula in the image is cyclopentanecarboxylic acid. The Latex tag for this chemical formula would be:

```latex
\text{Cyclopentanecarboxylic acid}
```

If you want to write the chemical structure in Latex, you can use the `chemfig` package:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{chemfig}
\begin{document}
\ch{C1(=O)O}
\end{document}
```

This will produce a chemical structure similar to the one in the image.
